ens but sometimes  this natural process  doesn't work as well as we'd like so you  need some exfoliants to come and give it  a bit of a kick along these days it  seems like every brand has a chemical  exfoliant but back then there were about  eight on the market and four of them  were from paula's choice they haven't  changed this formula that much but it  somehow still really stood its own after  more than a decade paula's choice is  just still really dominating when it  comes to salicylic acid formulas this is  still  the best formula i've tried and it's the  one that i keep going back to this is  the skincare product that i've had the  longest relationship with i try a lot of  skincare products and for most product  categories there'll be a few different  options that i end up really enjoying  and using regularly but for salicylic  acid this is the one that's sort of on  its own level for me and i've heard that  a lot of other people also feel the same  way paula's choice has a philosophy  where they always try to include other  supporting ingredients in their products  so this is actually one of their simpler  ones it's got humectants in the base  it's got a bit of green tea as well to  reduce irritation salicylic acid is a  little bit drying on the skin and it can  feel a bit tight while your skin adjusts  to it but i found that following up with  a hydrating tonal or moisturizer really  helps with this i love using this for  keeping my pores clear getting rid of  those little gray dots on your nose and  the pores i put this on with my fingers  and i mostly put it on my t-zone a few  times a week at night i also put it  sometimes a bit on my cheeks as well i  also used to use this in the morning  before but now i kind of just try to  keep my morning routine as simple as  possible this is the liquid version  which comes out very liquidy there's  also a lotion version but i've been so  happy with the liquid version that i've  never really had the urge to try the 