rks the best for them so  i think there is actually quite a lot of  variation with niacinamide formulas even  if they have the same percentage it  could also be the other ingredients in  this so the scoreboard glucoside in that  is a vitamin c derivative and it's one  of my favorites there are a whole bunch  of other supporting ingredients and  antioxidants in this too that also add  to this soothing effect so there's alan  toen and licorice extract paula's choice  really love the antioxidants and this  has a massive list of them the texture  is really watery and light it's a  water-based formula it's very easy to  incorporate into your routine because  it's so light it layers nicely under  everything else you can use it morning  or night i tend to use this every few  nights if my skin is particularly  irritated then sometimes i'll just use  this and nothing else for a few nights  maybe also with a moisturizer there is  also a 20 niacinamide which a lot of  people like if you want to go up even  higher with your niacinamide next up is  the point three percent retinol and two  percent pecucio treatment  this is one of my favorite retinal  products retinol is considered a gold  standard skincare ingredient it's a form  of vitamin a and it's an anti-aging  superstar ingredient back when i first  started on rational i made the mistake  of using a really big blob of the  poreless choice one percent retinol a  few nights in a row and that was a  massive mistake one percent is really  strong i thought my skin could handle it  because i was used to using 20 chemical  exfoliants with no big issues but  retinol is a whole different game i  think the really sneaky thing about  retinoid irritation is that it only  happens about a day and a half after  you've applied it with chemical  exfoliants you can usually tell right  after you've applied it that it's stingy  too much and you need to get it off but  with retinoids the next night your skin  will still usually mostly be fine 