tting  it in this separate section  if you don't already use a gentle  ascorbic acid i wouldn't recommend this  i would recommend using the c15 because  this is going to sting the c15 is a more  standard water-based ascorbic acid  product but my skin loves vitamin c and  i take forever to finish products so  this is perfect for me i like to apply  this by mixing it with a different  product first and then applying that  because i do find it a bit strong on its  own and i have this weird thing where i  don't like the feel of silicone skin  care products everyone else says that  silicones are cosmetically elegant and  silky so i am in the minority here i  usually mix a little blob of this with  the two percent bha liquid but you can  mix it in with any serum or moisturizer  paula's choice 10 as a lake acid booster  this is not actually allowed in  australia because azelaic acid is an  over-the-counter drug here but i really  like this because it has a really nice  smooth texture azolic acid products are  sometimes a bit paste like in texture  but this one is really light it feels a  lot more like a regular moisturizer  they've also put licorice and salicylic  acid in here to make a product that's  really good for evening out skin tone  and texture and unclogging pores so  those are my favorite pool of choice  products links to everything are in the  caption thank you so much to paula's  choice for sponsoring this video follow  paula's favorite youtuber on everything  skincare science video should be popping  up here and here if you want to keep  watching

